  "id": "COMPOUND:23226 - PROTEIN:4968",
  "verbalization": "Epi-actephilol A is shown to have a target relationship with Raji and MOVP-3, both of which are targets of complex compounds with distinct structural features. The evidence suggests that Epi-actephilol A may act on Raji through a pathway involving (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, which in turn targets ZR-75-1. Similarly, Epi-actephilol A is linked to MOVP-3, which targets ZR-75-1 via a different compound. These findings indicate that Epi-actephilol A may exert its biological effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of a target compound, which then interacts with ZR-75-1. The shared target ZR-75-1 suggests a potential role for Epi-actephilol A in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to this cell line. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Epi-actephilol A influences a downstream pathway that ultimately affects ZR-75-1.",
